@bio:

	Tim Eipert is a Research Assistant on the edition project
	<i>Corpus Monodicum: Die einstimmige Musik des lateinischen
	Mittelalters</i> and is working on his PhD at the 
	Julius-Maximilians-Universität Würzburg. He completed his
	Master's in Musicology in 2020 with a thesis on the
	automated segmentation of medieval chants. His dissertation
	investigates the transmission of medieval chant using
	computational methods, including Bayesian inference and
	network analysis. He is broadly interested in how
	humanities questions can be modelled computationally, with
	current work spanning medieval chant, digital editing, and
	jazz improvisation.

@@END: BIO